            <ArticleTitle>[Idiopathic progressive bilateral ureteral stenosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>201-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To report one case of progressive bilateral ureteral stenosis without demonstrable etiologic cause.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We diagnosed and treated a 73-year-old female patient who developed progressive bilateral distal ureteral stenosis without a demonstrable cause.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Surgery was carried out and the pathologic study showed a bilateral ureteral stenosis secondary to fibrosis and chronic unspecific inflammation.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Idiopathic ureteral stenosis is a rare clinical picture, more if progressive and bilateral.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
